## 11. Number of Ways to Move the Ball Out of the Grid

```python
def paths(m, n, N, i, j):
    if i < 0 or i >= m or j < 0 or j >= n:
        return 1
    if N == 0:
        return 0

    return (paths(m, n, N-1, i+1, j) +
            paths(m, n, N-1, i-1, j) +
            paths(m, n, N-1, i, j+1) +
            paths(m, n, N-1, i, j-1))

m = int(input("Rows: "))
n = int(input("Columns: "))
N = int(input("Steps: "))
i = int(input("Start Row: "))
j = int(input("Start Column: "))

print("Ways =", paths(m, n, N, i, j))
```
